  "title": "Fae Realm - Project: Gorgon Wiki",
  "main_content": "Fae Realm\nFrom Project: Gorgon Wiki\nJump to:\nnavigation\n,\nsearch\nFae Realm\nMap of Fae Realm (click for larger size)\nConnects to\nWinter Nexus\nTemperature:\nNormal\nArea Level\n70-80\n400px\nDistant Terminal\n- You can faintly hear bees buzzing.\n“\nA new explorable area has been added to the game! It's for those hardy adventurers who can already survive the dangers of\nGazluk\n. Being another plane of existence, it's not especially easy to reach. There is an entry method via the\nWinter Nexus\ndungeon, and there is also a way in via one of the caves in\nGazluk\n.\nThis area is a work in progress -- it will eventually also be the starting location for the playable fairy race, so you'll notice a few empty shop stalls, some suspiciously empty ruins, etc., which will be filled in later.\n—\nGame updates/2019-08-25\nThe\nFae Realm\nis actually one of many Fae Realms ruled over by whichever Fairy Court holds the throne. With the recent changeover to the Winter Court, the Winter Queen has been making advances to subjugate all other Fae. In this\nFae Realm\n, accessible through the\nWinter Nexus\nand a one-way portal chest from\nAmaluk Valley Cave\n, a resistance to the Winter Queen hides, aided by one aspect of\nAgrashab\n.\nNeighboring Regions\nWinter Nexus\nA rocky, troll infested cavern captured by the Winter Court. This dungeon has split the\nFae Realm\nfrom\nSun Vale\n.\nSun Vale\nA one-way shortcut to\nSun Vale\nin the form of a small portal can be found in the southwest corner of the Fel-Dasculan Ruins.\nOnly adventurers who are in the form of a\nFairy\nor\nRabbit\ncan use the portal.\nFae must first complete the quest\nElven Sketches\nto access the portal.\nPoints of Interest\nFel-Dasculan Ruins\nA ruined town on the northern side of the zone where many NPCs can be found.\n“\nThe fairies are squatting in the ruins of a much older fairy outpost, Fel-Dasculan. It was never very big or very important though.\n—\nAgrashab\nBee Hives\nAcross the\nFae Realm\n, large Bee Hives have sprung up, home to native and tended bees. Some of these hives posses enough sentience to offer quests to Fairies, while others will unleash waves of monsters on groups who try and interact with them.\nWinter Court Navy Exploration Site\nWinter Court fairies have staged and invasion of this\nFae Realm\nfrom the Winter Court Navy nethership Wintertide. The environment has been frozen around their encampment.\nFae Mollusc\nFae Mollusc\nare large molluscs native to the\nFae Realm\nwhich can be milked by passing travelers, similar to the tamed cows of\nAlharth\n.\nThere are 10\nFae Mollusc\nspread across the\nFae Realm\n.\nEach\nFae Mollusc\ncan be milked every 24 hours.\nFae Molluscs\nproduce\nFae Mollusc Slime\n, the key ingredient of\nFae Silk\n.\nBeast Forms\nare unable to milk\nFae Molluscs\n.\nHowever, a\nSpirit Fox\nusing illusion, strangely enough, can milk them.\n25 levels of\nFish and Snail Anatomy\nis required to milk a\nFae Mollusc\n. An\nEmpty Bottle\nmust be available, which will be filled during milking.\nTeleportation Circles\nThere are 0 Council constructed\nTeleportation Circles\nin the\nFae Realm\n.\nThere are 2\nmushroom circles\nin the\nFae Realm\n.\nIn the Fel-Dasculan Ruins.\nAt Ogamboe's ruins in the southeast, west of the Winter Court controlled area.\nMeditation Arches\nThere are 6\nMeditation Arches\nin the\nFae Realm\nregion. The provided\nMeditation Combos\nare:\nToss and Barrage\n- West arch.\nFiery Cobra\n- South arch.\nCrowd Surprise\n- Southeast arch.\nWrath of the Fist\n- Central arch.\nNervewreck\n- East arch.\nBruising Strike\n- North arch.\nDungeons\nThe Wintertide\nWinter Nexus\nWinter Nexus\nA frigid cave that acts as one of many Nexus systems between realms. The\nWinter Nexus\nis a stable path between the\nFae Realm\nand the region of\nSun Vale\n.\nThe Wintertide\nThe Wintertide\nis a Winter Court nethership found high above the\nFae Realm\n. A heavily guarded security portal to reach the ship can be found in the southeast corner of the region.\nAccessing\nThe Wintertide\nrequires a\nTransport Security Card\n.\nFae Realm Inhabitants\nFriendly NPCs\nAgrashab/Fae Realm\nBackfat\nBeehive\nBendith the Banished\nCrelpin\nFelmer\nFloxie\nGlowing Sphere\nMidge the Apothecary\nNoita the Green\nOgamboe\nPegast\nRaina\nSolgribue\nUriana\nFriendly NPCs in Fae Realm Dungeons\nEnsign Cricket\nEvent NPCs\nShovel Dispenser\nFoes\nBasilisk Controller\nBlinding Wasp\nBloodhunter Bee\nCarnivine\nCavorting Pixie\nDeinonychus\nElite Troll Trooper\nFae Bear\nFae Bee\nFae Panther\nFae Rhino\nFeral Bogeyman\nFey Ocelot\nFire Droach\nFire Elemental\nFire Spider\nFreezing Tornado\nFrost Hippogriff\nHatchling Deinonychus\nMarrowchomp\nNibbling Sprout\nOpportunistic Blinding Wasp\nOpportunistic Turret Wasp\nPhoenix\nPixie\nShocking Droach\nSkeleton Infiltrator\nSkeleton Intruder\nSpriggan Weed\nTroll Honeytender\nTrue Barghest\nTurret Wasp\nWild Turkey\nWinter Court Frostmaker\nWinter Court Scout\nWinter Court Soldier\nWinter Troll\nWinter War-Troll\nWintering Rhino\nSpecial Foes\nAncient Cold Elemental\nAncient Fire Elemental\nAncient Nature Elemental\nBeeoenix\nLethargy Puck\nMechanics\nDay/Night Cycle\nThe Fae Realm has a unique day/night cycle that does not follow the normal cycle of Alharth. Instead, the day/night status \"flips\" at random intervals, with a chiming sound. This cycle has a large effect on activities;\nOgamboe\n, for instance, is only available at night, and several resource node and enemy spawns are tied to either day or night.\nDaytime Enemy Spawns\nShocking Droaches\nWinter War Trolls\nPhoenices\nDeinonychus (needs confirmation)\nNighttime Enemy Spawns\nFire Droaches\nBasilisk Controllers\nShocking Droaches\nFire Spiders (needs confirmation)\nHarvestables\nInsects\nCrimsonfelt Wings\n(Nighttime)\nIcebreeze Moth Wings\n(Nighttime)\nShimmerwing Wings\n(Daytime)\nFruit\nPear\nPeach\nSprigganberries\nPlants\nCantaloupe Seedling\n(Daytime) (Foraging 70)\nBasil Seedling\n(Nighttime)\nTulip Seeds\n(Daytime)\nMushrooms\nCharged Mycelium\n(Nighttime)\nFly Amanita\n(Daytime)\nPixie's Parasol\n(Nighttime)\nMiscellaneous\nShiny Plate\nAncient Silver Coin\nFae Mollusc Slime\nfrom\nFae Molluscs\nCrystal Ice\n(From Ice Blocks. Often gives 8-10)\nEvents\nActivity Quests\nHorse Thieves (Ilmari)\nGallery\nFaeRealmFireMountain.png\nOne of many hills in the Fae Realm, this one is on fire!\nTrivia\nThe\nFae Realm\nwas added on August 25, 2019.\nRetrieved from \"\nhttp://wiki.projectgorgon.com/w/index.php?title=Fae_Realm&oldid=199064\n\"\nCategories\n:\nPages with broken file links\nDomesticated Animal\nZones",
